      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given truth table represents OR gate.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0179_8c88962566d2.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 84px;\" /></p><p>Its boolean algebra is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></math>,&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are input and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> is output.</p><p>OR&nbsp;gate gives output <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> if any one of its input is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
  }
